.TH LIGHTXR-GREETER 1 "2026-10-21" "de-xr" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lightxr\-greeter \- local and OpenXR display\-manager greeter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
/usr/local/libexec/lightxr/lightxr\-greeter [OPTIONS]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the native login interface. FLTK 1.4.5 is the default build; Qt6 is selected explicitly with CMake -DDE_XR_TOOLKIT=Qt6. In production the display manager supplies the authentication channel. The broker and presenter provide a curved XR panel about two metres ahead, controller pointing and an on\-screen keyboard.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-\-demo"
Preview without a LightDM/PAM connection. Authentication is disabled.
.TP
.B "\-\-windowed"
Use a window rather than the default fullscreen local view.
.TP
.B "\-\-bridge PATH"
Select the seat broker socket; default /run/lightxr\-broker/bridge.sock.
.TP
.B "\-\-help"
Show options.
.TP
.B "\-\-screenshot FILE"
FLTK diagnostic: write a PPM image of the greeter and exit. Implies demo mode;
no credentials are submitted. Requires a graphical display.
.SH FILES
The default FLTK build loads GNU Unifont from
/usr/local/share/lightxr/fonts/unifont-17.0.04.pcf, with a source-tree fallback
for local development. The Qt6 alternative embeds its font resource.
.SH EXAMPLES
\&./build/lightxr\-greeter \-\-demo \-\-windowed
.SH SEE ALSO
lightxr(8)
